$DIR/test.p:88:13: expected ';', found '{'
    Statements end at the end of a line, or at a semicolon. The parser found the
    end of one statement and then more text on the same line that does not start
    a new one. This usually means a missing operator, comma or bracket, or two
    statements on one line.
    (see "Semicolons" in the Plutonium spec, section 4.3)
    (run "pluto explain E1004" for a longer explanation)
